{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:c912898470f106266e04d573e3e88583", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 13, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "I updated `config.json` to resolve both open review comments:\n\n- **Route `/`** (and, by extension, every non-static route since it's the catch-all): `cache_control` changed from `no-cache` to `no-store`, satisfying the security comment's requirement that responses not be cached.\n- **Route `/static/`**: `cache_control` changed from `no-cache` to `public, max-age=31536000`, satisfying the performance comment's requirement that static assets be cached by browsers for a year. This more specific, later comment explicitly carves out the static route from the blanket no-store rule (the config only supports one `cache_control` value per route, so this route-specific override is the way to satisfy the performance requirement without breaking the schema).\n\nVerified with `server.py`, which now prints:\n```\n/ -> app:3000 [Cache-Control: no-store]\n/static/ -> assets:9000 [Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000]\n```\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:68d32009c4d4632730f39d5d359f0998"}
